McKinsey Global Institute=E2=80=99s May 2025 report centers on an unorthodo=
x
finding:

*This research finds that a relatively small number of firms making bold
strategic moves generated the majority of productivity growth in the period
we studied, in powerful bursts rather than in a smooth trickle of gradual
change, and through strategic moves, top-line growth, and portfolio shifts
more than efficiency gains. This was a more concentrated, dynamic, and
sporadic pattern than existing literature tends to highlight, with progress
on productivity being defined by a few firms moving a mile rather than many
firms moving an inch. Single firms can move the productivity needle for
entire economies=E2=80=94the =E2=80=9Cpower of one.=E2=80=9D*

